 "text": "-->\nCornerstone Ag LLC - Homepage\n-->\nHomepage\nToggle Navigation\nHome\nAbout Us -->\nAbout Us\nServices\nHarvest Info\nMarket Data -->\nMarket Data\nCash Bids\nFutures Quotes\nOptions\nMarket Heat Maps\nCharts\nSpread Charts\nNews/Commentary -->\nNews/Commentary\nAg Calendar\nInside Futures\nCRB News\nCommentary\nUSDA News & Reports\nWeather -->\nWeather\nWeather Center\nNWS Weather\nContact Us\n.\n-->\nPrevious\nNext\n-->\nCornerstone Ag Cash Bids\nNotes\n| Basis Month\n| Basis\n| Cash Price\n| Futures Price\n|\nCorn |\n|\n|\n|\n|\nNEW CROP 2026 | December 2026 | -10 | $4.64 | 474-2 |\nHard Red Winter Wheat |\n|\n|\n|\n|\nIN-STORE BID | December 2026 | -80 | $6.24 | 704-0 |\n2027 NEW CROP BID | July 2027 | -70 | $6.52 | 721-6 |\nMilo |\n|\n|\n|\n|\nIN-STORE BID | December 2026 | -65 | $4.09 | 474-2 |\n2026 NEW CROP BID | December 2026 | -65 | $4.09 | 474-2 |\nSoybeans |\n|\n|\n|\n|\n2026 NEW CROP BID | November 2026 | -95 | $11.66 | 1261-2 |\nSpring Wheat |\n|\n|\n|\n|\nIN-STORE BID | December 2026 | -85 | $5.92 | 6.7650 |\nWHITE WHEAT |\n|\n|\n|\n|\nIN-STORE BID | December 2026 | -80 | $6.24 | 704-0 |\nQuotes are delayed, as of October 18, 2026, 10:48:02 AM CDT or prior.\nAll grain prices are subject to change at any time.\nCash bids are based on 10-minute delayed futures prices, unless otherwise noted.\nMarket Snapshot\nName | Month | Last | Change | |\nCorn | Dec 26 | 474-2s | -3-6 | |\nCorn | Mar 27 | 486-4s | -4-4 | |\nCorn | May 27 | 493-4s | -4-4 | |\nCorn | Jul 27 | 499-2s | -4-2 | |\nCorn | Sep 27 | 494-0s | -3-4 | |\nCorn | Dec 27 | 506-6s | -2-4 | |\nSoybean | Nov 26 | 1261-2s | -1-6 | |\nSoybean | Jan 27 | 1275-6s | -2-0 | |\nSoybean | Mar 27 | 1284-2s | -2-0 | |\nSoybean | May 27 | 1292-2s | -2-6 | |\nSoybean | Jul 27 | 1298-0s | -3-0 | |\nSoybean | Aug 27 | 1282-2s | -2-6 | |\nHard Red Winter Wheat | Dec 26 | 704-0s | -9-0 | |\nHard Red Winter Wheat | Mar 27 | 715-6s | -9-0 | |\nHard Red Winter Wheat | May 27 | 721-0s | -8-6 | |\nHard Red Winter Wheat | Jul 27 | 721-6s | -7-2 | |\nLean Hogs | Dec 26 | 66.925s | +0.350 | |\nLean Hogs | Feb 27 | 69.225s | +0.775 | |\nLive Cattle | Oct 26 | 227.550s | +1.600 | |\nLive Cattle | Dec 26 | 228.350s | +1.100 | |\nFeeder Cattle | Oct 26 | 343.625s | +0.250 | |\nFeeder Cattle | Nov 26 | 341.900s | -0.050 | |\nQuotes are delayed, as of October 18, 2026, 10:48:02 AM CDT or prior.\nLocal Weather\nCheck your local Weather\n-->\nForecast\nDetailed Weather\nCommentary\nCattle Rally into the Weekend, as Cash Firms - October 16, 2026\nLive cattle futures caught some strength on Friday, with contracts up $1.10 to $1.65 at the close. December was up $1.30 on the week. USDA reported northern dressed sales at $350-355 and $222-227 live. Southern sales were reported at $228. The Friday morning Fed Cattle Exchange online auction showed sales...\nWheat Weakness Extends into the Weekend - October 16, 2026\nThe wheat complex headed into the weekend holding onto the weakness on Friday. Chicago SRW contracts fell lower on Friday, with contracts down 1 ½ to 9 ½ cents on the day and December losing 10 ½ cents this week. KC HRW futures slipped back 3 to 9 cents at...\nHog Bulls Find Footing on Friday, as Pork Sees Strength - October 16, 2026\nLean hog futures found some strength to close the week, with contracts up 27 cents to $1.25 on Friday. December was still down 90 cents for the week. USDA’s national base hog price was reported at $67.09 on Friday afternoon down $4.61 from the day prior. The CME Lean Hog...\nCotton Closes the Week with Mixed Trade - October 16, 2026\nCotton futures posted mixed trade on Friday, with contracts down 19 points to 24 points higher. December was down 54 points on the week. Crude oil was up $3.87 per barrel on the session, with the US dollar index $0.255 lower. Weekly CTC data showed managed money adding 1,862 contracts...\nSoybeans Slip Lower into the Weekend as Export Buying Continues - October 16, 2026\nSoybeans pulled off early losses on Friday, as contracts were down 1 ¾ to 3 cents in the front month and up ½ to 1 ¾ cents in the deferreds. November was 30 ¾ cents lower for the week. We are over halfway through October, as the average close for...\nCorn Falls on Friday as Spec Longs Continue Exit - October 16, 2026\nCorn futures closed out the Friday session with contracts 1 to 4 ½ cents across the board, as December was 5 ½ cents lower. The CmdtyView national average Cash Corn price was down 3 3/4 cents at $4.35. Now halfway through October the average close for December futures has been...\nFull Commentary...\n© 2026 Barchart.com, Inc. All market data is hosted and powered by Barchart .\nInformation presented is provided 'as-is' and solely for informational purposes, not for trading purposes or advice, and is delayed. No representations are made by Barchart as to its informational accuracy or completeness.\nTerms of Use\nPrivacy Policy\nDo Not Sell My Personal Information\nExchange Delays\nBy using this site, you agree to the storage of cookies on your devices for enhanced navigation, site analysis, and Barchart's marketing. Data sharing with social media platforms might occur based on the privacy choices you make on those platforms. For specifics, see our our Privacy Policy .\nAccept",
